# Build context exclusions.
#
# The Dockerfile needs exactly two things: requirements.txt and src/.  Everything
# else here is either dead weight sent to the daemon or, worse, local state that
# COPY would bake into the image.
#
# The dangerous entries are the SQLite ones.  src/data/eos_connect.db is gitignored
# but gitignore has no bearing on the build context, so a local `docker compose
# build` used to copy the developer's own database to /app/data/eos_connect.db in
# the image.  The ./data bind mount normally hides it, but a `docker run` without
# -v would start on someone else's configuration.  Dockerfile's `mkdir -p /app/data`
# recreates the empty directory, so excluding it costs nothing.

# Version control and IDE state
.git/
.gitignore
.github/
.vscode/
.mypy_cache/
.pytest_cache/

# Virtualenvs and bytecode
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
**/__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# Local SQLite state — must never reach the image (see note above)
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
src/data/

# Local bootstrap config and runtime dumps.  src/json/readme.md is deliberately
# kept so the directory still exists in the image: eos_connect.py writes
# optimize_request.json / optimize_response.json into it at runtime.
src/config.yaml
src/config.yaml.bak
src/config.bak.yaml
src/json/*.json

# Tests, docs and tooling — not shipped
tests/
docs/
scripts/
pytest.ini
requirements-dev.txt
*.md
CLAUDE.md

# Compose file itself
docker-compose.yml
